{"seq":3,"slug":"ideas-and-methods","title":"丹尼尔·卡尼曼·思想与方法","stage":"DONE","category":"daniel-kahneman","categoryLabel":"丹尼尔·卡尼曼","chapterCount":3,"docCount":6,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/daniel-kahneman/ideas-and-methods","rating":{"composite":3.75,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.4,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":4.67,"strategic":3.67},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"hubDir":"/Users/wangyang.learnwy/learnwy/learnwy/l-doc-hub/hubs/famous-people/07_daniel-kahneman/3_ideas-and-methods","introHtml":"<h1 id=\"思想与方法\">思想与方法</h1><p>本卷剖析丹尼尔·卡尼曼思想中那些更具方法论与哲学意味的层面：他对人类心智之&quot;有限理性&quot;的根本判断、他晚年对&quot;何为幸福&quot;的重新发问，以及他对&quot;科学家如何对抗自身偏误&quot;的制度性回应。如果说他的核心贡献是一组具体的发现，那么本卷讲的是支撑这些发现的底层世界观与求真方法。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本卷-vs-兄弟卷的分工\">本卷 vs 兄弟卷的分工</h2><p>本卷刻意与同人物的其他兄弟卷错开，避免重复展开：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>具体的发现机制——启发法、各类认知偏误、前景理论、损失厌恶、系统1与系统2——属于 <a href=\"../core-contributions/\">核心贡献</a>，本卷只引用、不重述。</li>\n<li>这些思想的载体（《思考，快与慢》《噪声》、诺贝尔奖、里程碑论文）属于 <a href=\"../major-works/\">代表成就</a>。</li>\n<li>思想对经济学、政策、日常生活的下游影响属于 <a href=\"../influence-and-legacy/\">影响与遗产</a>。</li>\n<li>对这些思想的批评、复制危机与理性之辩属于 <a href=\"../controversies-and-appraisal/\">争议与评价</a>。</li>\n<li>人物的生平脉络属于 <a href=\"../life-and-times/\">生平与时代</a>。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>一句话：<strong>核心贡献回答&quot;卡尼曼发现了什么&quot;，本卷回答&quot;这些发现背后的人性观与求真观是什么&quot;。</strong></p>\n<h2 id=\"三章结构与推荐学习路径\">三章结构与推荐学习路径</h2><p>本卷分三章，建议顺序阅读，因为后一章常以前一章为前提：</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>第一章·易错的心智</strong>——奠定世界观。先读 <a href=\"the-fallible-mind/bounded-rationality\">有限理性</a>（从西蒙到卡尼曼，人为何系统性偏离理性），再读 <a href=\"the-fallible-mind/intuition-and-its-limits\">直觉及其局限</a>（直觉这一具体捷径在什么条件下可信）。</li>\n<li><strong>第二章·经验与记忆</strong>——把方法论转向幸福。先读 <a href=\"experience-vs-memory/two-selves\">两个自我</a>（经验自我 vs 记忆自我的根本区分），再读 <a href=\"experience-vs-memory/peak-end-rule\">峰终定律</a>（这种区分的精确规律与判决性实验）。</li>\n<li><strong>第三章·关于思考的思考</strong>——回到求真方法。先读 <a href=\"thinking-about-thinking/the-effort-of-debiasing\">去偏的努力</a>（为何个体难以自救、要靠改造环境），再读 <a href=\"thinking-about-thinking/adversarial-collaboration\">对抗式合作</a>（如何用制度让科学家的偏误相互制衡）。</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"前置知识\">前置知识</h2><p>阅读本卷前，最好先理解 <a href=\"../core-contributions/two-systems/system-1-and-system-2\">系统1与系统2</a> 这一双系统框架——它是&quot;有限理性&quot;&quot;直觉&quot;&quot;去偏&quot;三篇共同的解释底座。若对启发法与具体偏误尚不熟悉，可先浏览 <a href=\"../core-contributions/heuristics-and-biases/cognitive-biases\">认知偏误</a>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"贯穿本卷的一条主线\">贯穿本卷的一条主线</h2><p>六篇看似分散，实则被一条线串起：<strong>人无法靠意识与意志克服自身的认知局限，因此求真必须依靠外部的结构。</strong> 有限理性指出局限的存在，直觉研究划出局限的边界，两个自我与峰终定律揭示连&quot;幸福&quot;也被局限扭曲，去偏与对抗式合作则给出唯一务实的出路——不改造大脑，而改造大脑所处的环境与制度。读完本卷，你会理解卡尼曼为何被称为&quot;谦逊的科学家&quot;：他对人性局限的诊断极其冷峻，给出的药方却极其务实。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-fallible-mind","title":"易错的心智","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/daniel-kahneman/ideas-and-methods/the-fallible-mind","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"bounded-rationality","title":"有限理性","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/daniel-kahneman/ideas-and-methods/the-fallible-mind/bounded-rationality"},{"seq":2,"slug":"intuition-and-its-limits","title":"直觉及其局限","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/daniel-kahneman/ideas-and-methods/the-fallible-mind/intuition-and-its-limits"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"experience-vs-memory","title":"经验与记忆","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/daniel-kahneman/ideas-and-methods/experience-vs-memory","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"two-selves","title":"两个自我","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/daniel-kahneman/ideas-and-methods/experience-vs-memory/two-selves"},{"seq":2,"slug":"peak-end-rule","title":"峰终定律","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/daniel-kahneman/ideas-and-methods/experience-vs-memory/peak-end-rule"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"thinking-about-thinking","title":"关于思考的思考","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/daniel-kahneman/ideas-and-methods/thinking-about-thinking","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-effort-of-debiasing","title":"去偏的努力","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/daniel-kahneman/ideas-and-methods/thinking-about-thinking/the-effort-of-debiasing"},{"seq":2,"slug":"adversarial-collaboration","title":"对抗式合作","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/daniel-kahneman/ideas-and-methods/thinking-about-thinking/adversarial-collaboration"}]}]}